<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened runtime entitlements for the Developer ID build (scripts/release-macos-signed.sh).
  The app is not sandboxed, so network, Keychain and file access need no entitlement here.
  Each key below relaxes one hardened runtime check; keep this list as short as it can be.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    The .NET JIT compiles IL to machine code at run time into MAP_JIT memory. Without this the
    hardened runtime refuses that mapping and CoreCLR does not start at all ("Failed to create
    CoreCLR, HRESULT 0x80070008"; measured on this bundle on September 26, 2026). Required.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <!--
    Not included: com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory (writable and executable
    memory outside MAP_JIT). Tested on September 26, 2026 with .NET 10: ad-hoc hardened-runtime
    bundles (codesign --options runtime -s -) carrying only the two keys in this file started
    in --script-worker mode and answered a request, both osx-arm64 natively and osx-x64 under
    Rosetta. The same two bundles also opened the main window with an empty data directory
    and ran for 10 seconds (Avalonia.Native, Skia and SQLite loaded; no world connected).
    If a signed build crashes with a code-signing or memory-protection fault, add this key
    back first.
  -->
  <!--
    Library validation lets a process load only code signed by Apple or by its own team. The host
    loads libhostfxr, libcoreclr and the native libraries of NuGet packages (SkiaSharp, HarfBuzz,
    ONNX Runtime, SQLite, Avalonia.Native) with dlopen. The release script re-signs every one of
    them with the same Developer ID, which should satisfy validation on its own; this key keeps the
    app starting if a native library is ever loaded from outside the bundle or missed by signing.
    An ad-hoc signed test bundle does not start without it.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
